<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;">
      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What is box build?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Box build covers the assembly of the complete product around the populated circuit board, including enclosures, cables and harnesses, mechanical parts, sealing, functional test and final packing.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What does Hana’s box build include?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Hana supports enclosure and housing assembly, cable and wire-harness assembly, potting, mechanical integration and large box build.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Can Hana test the finished product, not just the board?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. Functional test can be carried out at the box-build level, with in-house development of product-specific test rigs. Testing can include wireless, GSM/cellular, GPS, Bluetooth (IoT), acoustic and more.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Can Hana ship finished products directly?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. Finished units can be drop-shipped on EXW, DDU or FOB terms.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How is box build different from PCBA?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">PCBA produces the populated circuit board. Box build integrates that board into the complete product, including enclosure, harnesses, mechanical parts, functional test and fulfillment.</div>
    </details>
